 - Completed phase 109 on 2026-06-15 by running a controlled one-site Coca-Cola smoke capture with `--no-save`. The command wrote `data/smoke_coca_cola_2026-06-15.csv` plus `data/captures/sites/www_coca_cola_com_20260615_043524/layer1.png` and local `layer1.html`; a synced DOM evidence excerpt is in `data/smoke_coca_cola_2026-06-15_dom_evidence.csv`. The capture environment produced valid screenshot/DOM evidence again, but the automated Layer 1 booleans missed visible OneTrust controls (`Allow All`, `Reject All`, and `Confirm My Choices`), so the row is an extraction/debugging signal rather than a final RQ1 score.
 - Completed phase 110 on 2026-06-15 by fixing the OneTrust pathway-recognition bug exposed by the Coca-Cola smoke. Root causes: `Confirm My Choices` was not classified as customize, `Close preference center` was misclassified, `Privacy Preference Center` could be treated as a false pathway label, click replay waited only 1 second for delayed CMP controls, and aria-labeled close buttons were not clickable through the text-only helper. Added red/green regressions in `tests/capture/test_agent.py` and `tests/capture/test_capture_site_integration.py`, updated `src/consent_audit/capture/agent.py`, and verified with a live `--no-save` Coca-Cola postfix smoke at `data/smoke_coca_cola_postfix_2026-06-15.csv`: accept/reject/customize/dismiss all `true`, gate `true`, tier `Exemplary`.
 - Completed phase 111 on 2026-06-16 by doing a fact-consistency review against `git status`, `git log`, `research-status`, the June 15 smoke audit, and the postfix smoke CSV. Corrected stale wording in `docs/research/june15_coca_cola_smoke_audit_2026-06-15.md` and `docs/research/full_project_audit_2026-06-15.md` so they no longer imply the OneTrust blocker remains unresolved after the post-fix smoke.
+- Completed phase 112 on 2026-06-18 by checking the current PR/research state and adding `docs/research/today_work_note_2026-06-18.md`. Evidence checked: GitHub PR #4 is merged, `research-status` still reports sanity `ready`, cycle `completed`, 42 audit reports, 20 longitudinal summaries, and 8 pending CMP confirmations. Linked the new note from `README.md` and `docs/research/week2_checkin_index_2026-06-06.md`.
